  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Cobra (Middle section only)** (1 review): The reviewer, who says they attended, notes the band played Cobra [3]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **How Do You Know**: rare: 10 archived performances [8]\n- **Death Is The Easy Way**: rare: 14 archived performances [8]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **mmj2004-05-16oktava.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 15 songs; 94 min; rated 4.5/5 by 4 [1]. Said about its sound: The Oktava recording is somewhat heavy in the low end, which the reviewer says suits MMJ's sound; The Oktava microphones give a somewhat bass-heavy recording [3][5]\n- **mmj2004-05-16.mc012.16bit**: source not stated; 15 songs; 94 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [2]. Said about its sound: This recording sounds good, and Jim's voice sits well in it [7]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Unlike many terrible-sounding early MMJ recordings, this one sounds good and captures the band's essence [7]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **mmj2004-05-16oktava.flac16**: taped by Mike B.; transferred by Mike B.; source: Oktava MC012 / Core Sound Binaurals (4 mic mix) > Edirol UA5 > Optical > Nomad JB3 (@ 48KHz) > Sound Forge 6.0 (Resample to 44.1KHz with anti-alias filter /… [1]. Also: A reviewer says they taped this show; the version posted was in compressed MP3/OGG format; The reviewer sees no minidisc or other lossy gear in this recording's lineage [5][6]\n- **mmj2004-05-16.mc012.16bit**: taped by Mike B; transferred by Mike B; source: Oktava MC012 / Core Sound Binaurals (4 mic mix) > Edirol UA5 > Optical > Nomad JB3 (@ 48KHz) [2]",
